UPDATE companies SET description='Mid-South Wire Products Inc. was founded in 1967 by John T. Johnson, Sr. in Nashville, Tennessee. The company remains family-owned, now led by John T. Johnson, Jr., and operates a second facility in Scott City, Missouri. Its origins trace to a single “sidewinder” bull-block drawing machine acquired in 1964, which still sits outside the Nashville offices as a reminder of the firm’s humble start.

The company manufactures carbon steel wire products including wire rod, bright basic wire, plating-quality wire, nitrogen-wiped galvanized wire (Class 1–4 per ASTM A-641), and welded wire mesh for concrete reinforcement. Production runs on more than 30 wire-drawing machines, supported by a modern pickle room, a high-speed Morgan Koch multi-pass drawing line, a galvanizing line, and an overhead railcar-unloading system. A dedicated tractor-trailer fleet and a private barge operation on the Cumberland River provide direct shipping options.

Mid-South Wire serves automotive seating suppliers such as Lear Seigler, Hoover Universal, and Johnson Controls, as well as cable manufacturer Copperweld and shelving producer Lee Rowan (later Rubbermaid). Its customer base spans the automotive, construction, cable, and industrial storage sectors throughout the Southeast and beyond.

The firm differentiates itself with a just-in-time delivery model built on in-stock inventory, company-owned trucks, and river barge access, promising on-time delivery for every order. Family values and a “can-do” culture—evident in the rapid recovery after the 1975 Cumberland River flood—underpin its commitment to service and continuous equipment investment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire drawing", "Bright basic wire manufacturing", "Plating quality wire manufacturing", "Galvanizing (nitrogen-wiped, Class 1-4 per ASTM A-641)", "Wire mesh manufacturing (concrete reinforcement)", "Pickling / acid cleaning", "Rod yard operations", "Railcar unloading", "Barge transportation", "Truck fleet delivery", "Just-in-time delivery"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Construction", "Cable manufacturing", "Shelving and storage"], "materials": ["Low carbon steel", "Medium carbon steel", "Steel wire rod", "Bright basic steel", "Plating-grade steel", "Galvanized steel"], "equipment": ["\"Sidewinder\" bull block wire-drawing machine (historical)", "Morgan Koch high-speed multi-pass drawing machine", "Pickle room (acid cleaning)", "Galvanizing line", "Overhead railcar-unloading system", "Tractor-trailer fleet", "Barge system on Cumberland River", "Railroad siding"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Just-in-time delivery model with in-stock inventory and company-owned fleet", "Private barge system on the Cumberland River for economical shipping", "More than 30 wire-drawing machines enabling a broad product range", "Family-owned since 1967 with second-generation leadership", "On-time delivery guarantee"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1967 by John T. Johnson, Sr. -> /about", "Family-owned business -> /about", "Headquartered in Nashville, Tennessee with second location in Scott City, Missouri -> /about", "More than 30 wire drawing machines -> /about", "Products: bright basic wire, plating quality wire, galvanized wire, wire mesh -> /", "Galvanized wire Class 1-4 per ASTM A-641 -> /", "Automotive customers: Lear Seigler, Hoover Universal, Johnson Controls -> /about", "Cable manufacturer Copperweld and shelving company Lee Rowan -> /about", "ISO 9001 compliance mentioned in quality technician job posting -> /quality", "Equipment: Morgan Koch drawing machine, pickle room, galvanizing line, overhead railcar-unloading system -> /about", "Barge system on Cumberland River and tractor-trailer fleet -> /about", "Just-in-time delivery model -> /about", "Sidewinder bull block machine acquired 1964 -> /about", "Railroad siding at Visco Drive location -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mid-South Wire is a leading maker of carbon steel wire.", "founded_year": "1967", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mid-south-wire-products-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Middle Tennessee Solar LLC operates from Clarksville, Tennessee.

The firm functions as a solar equipment distributor, stocking photovoltaic panels, battery storage, inverters, charge controllers, and associated mounting hardware and cabling. It carries product lines from EG4 Electronics, AIMS Power, Schneider Electric, and Growatt, among others. The company reports more than 500 clients served, over 366 projects completed, and relationships with 85-plus business partners. No facility size or employee count is published.

Customers include DIY enthusiasts, homesteaders, residential contractors, and small commercial installers building off-grid, grid-tied, or hybrid solar systems.

Middle Tennessee Solar emphasizes a curated product selection — only brands the team would use in their own homes — and avoids pre-bundled kits that inflate costs. It promotes direct access to technical support and fast local shipping from its Clarksville location as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar panel distribution", "Battery storage distribution", "Inverter distribution", "Charge controller distribution", "Mounting hardware and cabling supply", "Solar system design consultation", "Residential solar package configuration", "Off-grid solar kit assembly", "Grid-tied solar system component supply"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Off-grid power systems", "Renewable energy", "DIY solar", "Contractor solar supply"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Curated product selection: only brands the company trusts for its own installations", "No pre-bundled kits or inflated markups", "Fast local shipping from Clarksville, Tennessee", "Direct technical support without clueless sales representatives", "Component-level guidance to help customers avoid guesswork"], "facts_used": ["Company location: Clarksville, Tennessee -> /", "Founded in 2019 (Since 2019) -> /", "Business type: solar equipment supplier/distributor -> /", "Brands carried: EG4 Electronics, AIMS Power, Schneider Electric, Growatt -> /", "Customer types: DIYers, homesteaders, contractors, homeowners -> /", "Scale metrics: 500+ happy clients, 366+ projects completed, 85+ business partners -> /", "Differentiators: no bloated bundles, no clueless sales reps, fast local shipping, curated brands -> /", "Services: consultation, residential packages, component supply -> /", "Database founded_year: 2011 (appears to refer to Growatt) -> db", "Database HQ: Clarksville, Tennessee -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We''re a solar equipment supplier in Clarksville, TN that stocks only the parts you actually need.", "founded_year": "2019", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='middle-tennessee-solar-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Midian Electronics was founded in 1975 by Chuck Soulliard in Tucson, Arizona. The company began by specializing in after-market 2805/1500 Hz and 600/1500 Hz MTS pulse tone decoders, as well as SECODE SMART/IMTS/DTMF radio-telephone encoders-decoders with ANI. Its name derives from "Miniature Digital and Analog," reflecting the focus on compact electronic modules for land mobile radio.

Today Midian designs and manufactures a broad line of radio communication products, including tone signaling modules (DTMF, pulse tone, two-tone, five-tone), voice security devices such as voice scramblers and AES-128 bit encryption, tone remote desk sets, termination panels, two-way radio interoperability switches, remote control and monitoring systems, fleet management, telephone interconnects, paging and alarm products, and plug-in modules for OEM radios. The company also offers in-house custom electronic circuit design, PCB layout, and product development services. All products are designed and built at its Tucson facility and carry a three-year parts and labor warranty.

Midian''s equipment serves public safety agencies (police, fire, ambulance), fleet operators (taxi, towing, fishing), government and military users, industrial and commercial businesses, and OEM radio manufacturers. Its interoperability solutions, for example, bridge LTE to VHF or connect Site Connect to P25 networks.

The company distinguishes itself by being the first to bring after-market MTS pulse tone decoders to market and by introducing the world''s first voice scrambler small enough to fit inside a portable two-way radio. Midian states its mission is to continue providing innovative, after-market products that improve the safety and versatility of two-way radio networks.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Tone signaling (DTMF, pulse tone, two-tone, five-tone encoders/decoders)", "Voice security (voice scramblers, AES-128 bit encryption)", "Tone remote desk sets and termination panels", "Two-way radio interoperability switching (voice bridge, cross-band repeater)", "Remote control and monitoring (pumps, generators, irrigation, lighting, fluid levels)", "Fleet management systems", "Telephone interconnect and radio-telephone interface", "Paging and alarm products", "Plug-in modules for OEM radios", "ANI (Automatic Number Identification) systems", "Custom electronic circuit design", "Custom PCB design and layout", "Product design and development"], "industries": ["Public safety (police, fire, ambulance)", "Fleet (taxi, towing, fishing)", "Government", "Industrial", "OEM (original equipment manufacturers)", "Military", "Commercial business"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First to market with after-market 2805/1500 Hz and 600/1500 Hz MTS pulse tone decoders", "World''s first voice scrambler small enough to fit inside a portable two-way radio", "Industry-leading 3-year parts and labor warranty on all products", "In-house electronic circuit design, custom PCB layout, and product development services", "All products designed and manufactured in Tucson, Arizona"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 by Chuck Soulliard in Tucson, Arizona -> /about-us", "Name from Miniature Digital and Analog -> /about-us", "First products: tone signaling modules for land mobile radio -> /about-us", "First after-market MTS pulse tone decoders -> /about-us", "1981: world''s first portable voice scrambler -> /about-us", "Product line includes tone remote, interoperability, ANI, encryption, remote control, fleet management, telephone interconnect, paging, OEM plug-ins -> / and /about-us", "Designed and built in Tucson, Arizona -> / and /about-us", "3-year parts and labor warranty -> / and /about-us", "In-house custom circuit design, PCB, product design -> /", "Industries: public safety, fleet, government, industrial, OEM, military, commercial -> /about-us", "Headquarters: 2030 N. Forbes Blvd. #101 Tucson, AZ 85745 -> / and /about-us", "Founded year 1975 from database -> db", "City/state Tucson, Arizona from database -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Midian Electronics manufactures products to improve the safety and versatility of your communication networks.", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='midian-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Midlands Packaging Corporation has operated from Lincoln, Nebraska since its founding on April 1, 1972. The company remains locally owned and managed, with sales offices across the Midwest in Dallas, Denver, Kansas City, Minneapolis, Omaha, St. Louis, and Sioux City.

The manufacturer produces folding cartons, corrugated containers, thermoformed plastics, laminated cartons, specialty boxes, and point-of-purchase displays. Structural design uses CAD linked to CAM, and the 170-person workforce averages 15 years of tenure.

Midlands serves retail and pharmaceutical customers requiring packaging that meets FDA regulations (21 CFR 176.180, 211.122) and Federal Specification PPP-B-566E, as well as food-industry clients covered by its SQF Level 1 certification. The quality system follows ANSI/ASQ Z1.4 sampling, and the plant holds FSC Chain of Custody certification.

The company emphasizes assigned account teams — each customer receives a dedicated sales person and service representative — and highlights its in-house die shop, long-tenured staff, and 100% recycling of production waste as operational differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['FSC Chain of Custody Certification (FSC® C009047)','SQF Code Edition 7.1 Level 1: Food Safety Fundamentals Certification (639544)','ANSI/ASQ Z1.4-2003/2008 sampling']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Folding carton manufacturing", "Corrugated container manufacturing", "Thermoformed plastics manufacturing (clamshells, blisters, tri-folds)", "Laminated carton manufacturing (single face corrugated, litho label)", "Specialty box manufacturing (set-up boxes, stayed boxes)", "Display manufacturing (custom trade show booths, POP displays)", "Structural design (CAD)", "Computer Aided Manufacturing (CAM)", "In-house die shop", "UV, aqueous, and specialty coatings", "Metallic, coin reactive, and UV inks", "Pre-print/post-print foil stamping", "Foil stock application", "Cello and poly window application", "Security tag insertion", "Label and IRC application", "Double stick tape application", "Insert application", "Sheeting (roll to sheet)", "Six-color printing with inline UV coating", "Die cutting", "Gluing", "100% recycling of production waste", "Quality inspection per ANSI/ASQ Z1.4", "FDA 21 CFR 176.180 and 211.122 compliance"], "industries": ["Retail", "Pharmaceutical", "Food"], "materials": ["Paper rolls", "UV coatings", "Aqueous coatings", "Specialty coatings", "Metallic inks", "Coin reactive inks", "UV inks", "Foil stock", "Cello window film", "Poly window film", "Security tags", "Labels", "IRC (instant redeemable coupons)", "Double stick tape", "Inserts", "Corrugated board", "Thermoformed plastics"], "equipment": ["KBA Rapida 105 printers (two)", "Four die cutters", "Four gluers", "Sheeter", "CAD/CAM system", "In-house die shop"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded April 1, 1972 -> /", "Headquarters Lincoln, Nebraska -> /", "Locally owned and operated -> /", "170 employees with average 15 years service -> /", "Produces folding cartons, corrugated containers, thermoformed plastics, laminated cartons, specialty boxes, displays -> /", "Four KBA Rapida 105 printers, six-color inline UV coating -> /", "Four die cutters, four gluers, sheeter -> /", "In-house die shop -> /", "CAD/CAM design -> /", "FSC Chain of Custody certification (2008) -> /", "SQF Code Edition 7.1 Level 1 certification (2014) -> /", "FDA 21 CFR 176.180, 211.122 compliance -> /", "Federal Specification PPP-B-566E compliance -> /", "ANSI/ASQ Z1.4 sampling -> /", "Assigned sales person and service representative per account -> /", "100% recycling of production waste -> /", "Sales offices in Dallas, Denver, Kansas City, Minneapolis, Omaha, St. Louis, Sioux City -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Midlands Packaging primarily produces folding cartons, corrugated containers, and thermoformed plastics.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "170", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["http://www.midlandspkg.com/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='midlands-packaging-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company provides engineering support to help customers finalize designs and develop effective manufacturing solutions.

Its manufacturing capabilities include straightening and cutting wire, fourslide and multislide forming, stamping, buffing, resistance, automatic, heli-arc and arc welding, CNC bending, drilling, threading, tapping, and assembly. An in-house tooling department supports production, and the company offers logistics support for inventory control as well as quick, cost-efficient prototype and sample production.

The company serves customers across a range of industries that require custom wire forms and stampings, though specific sectors are not detailed in its public materials.

Midwest Wire Products emphasizes value and satisfaction, backed by an ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system. Its differentiators include in-house tooling, logistics support, rapid prototyping, and engineering collaboration to optimize designs for manufacturability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire straightening and cutting", "Fourslide/multislide forming", "Stamping", "Buffing", "Resistance welding", "Automatic welding", "Heli-arc welding", "Arc welding", "CNC bending", "Drilling", "Threading", "Tapping", "Assembly", "Tooling design and fabrication", "Logistics and inventory management", "Prototyping and sample production"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tooling department", "Logistics support for cost-efficient inventory control", "Rapid, cost-efficient prototype and sample production", "Engineering support for design finalization and manufacturability", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Sturgeon Bay, Wisconsin -> db", "Company organized as LLC -> page /", "Full-service metal forming company specializing in custom wireforms and stampings -> page /", "Engineering support for design finalization -> page /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system -> page / and /about-us", "In-house tooling department -> page / and /about-us", "Logistics support for cost-efficient inventory control -> page / and /about-us", "Samples/prototypes produced quickly and cost efficiently -> page / and /about-us", "Capabilities: straightening and cutting wire, fourslide/multislide, stamping, buffing, resistance/automatic/heli-arc/arc welding, CNC bending, drilling, threading, tapping, assembly -> page /about-us", "Goal to produce value and satisfaction -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Midwest Wire Products is a full-service 