UPDATE companies SET description='Midwestern Wood Products Company has operated from Peoria, Illinois since its founding in 1968. The company traces its expertise to the development of the WOODGRID® Suspended Coffered Ceiling System, a wood-based drop-ceiling solution designed to replicate historic coffered aesthetics with modern installation methods.

The company manufactures the WOODGRID® system, which consists of main runners, cross tees, and drop-in coffer panels that create depth and architectural interest. The panels are removable, allowing access to mechanical and electrical systems above the ceiling. Midwestern Wood Products offers multiple styles, wood species, and finishes, and coordinates with Heritage Restoration and Design for custom finishing techniques such as antique painting. The system accommodates various ceiling conditions including high, low, cathedral, and basement heights, and integrates with lighting, venting, soffits, and home theater components.

The product serves both residential and commercial markets. In homes, it is used in libraries, studies, dens, offices, and basements where access to ductwork is needed. Commercial applications include restaurants, lobbies, and other venues where a non-commercial, cozy appearance is desired. The company notes that the system is suitable for new construction and remodel projects alike.

Midwestern Wood Products emphasizes that its WOODGRID® ceiling is American-made, affordable, and installs similarly to a standard metal grid system. The company also highlights its 40 years of experience in decorative wood drop ceilings and its ability to customize layouts for each space.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wood coffered ceiling manufacturing", "Suspended ceiling system design", "Custom finishing (stains, varnishes, antique painting)", "Integration with lighting, venting, and mechanicals", "Removable panel system for maintenance access"], "industries": ["Residential construction and remodeling", "Commercial construction", "Hospitality (restaurants, lobbies)", "Basement finishing", "Home theater installations"], "materials": ["Wood (various species)", "Tin panels", "Metal grid (15/16\")"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["American-made product", "Removable coffer panels for above-ceiling access", "Installs like a standard metal grid system", "Custom finishes via Heritage Restoration and Design", "Styles for cathedral, basement, and standard ceiling heights"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1968 -> db and page ''Family Owned Since 1968''", "Headquartered in Peoria, Illinois -> db", "Family-owned -> page", "Manufactures WOODGRID\u00ae Suspended Coffered Ceiling System -> page", "System includes removable coffer panels for access -> page", "Offers multiple styles, wood species, finishes -> page", "Partners with Heritage Restoration and Design for custom finishes -> page", "Serves residential and commercial markets -> page", "Applications include home libraries, basements, restaurants, lobbies -> page", "American-made, installs like metal grid -> page", "40 years of experience in decorative wood drop ceilings -> page"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today we have the WOODGRID\u00ae Suspended Coffered Ceiling System which is both elegant and affordable.", "founded_year": "1968", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='midwestern-wood-products-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mighty Auto Parts operates a wholesale distribution franchise in Henderson, Nevada. The Henderson location is managed by designated manager Scott Worrall and serves the local market with bilingual English and Spanish support.

The company distributes automotive replacement parts sourced from original-equipment manufacturers, carrying product lines that include brakes, filters, batteries, belts and tensioners, chemicals, hardware and fasteners, motor oil and lubricants, shop supplies, tire-service items, tools and equipment, wipers, and personal protection equipment. Beyond parts supply, the franchise provides value-added services such as professional inventory management, obsolescence protection, business consulting, customized technician training, an online catalog (MIC), a Rapid Rewards loyalty program, shop-management software, and marketing support.

Customers are exclusively professional automotive service providers — independent repair shops, dealership service departments, and fleet maintenance operations — in the Henderson area. The business model is strictly B2B wholesale; no retail or consumer sales are conducted at this location.

Mighty positions its differentiation on local accessibility and service depth: a dedicated representative is available on-site rather than through offshore call centers, and the combination of inventory management, technical support, and business expertise is intended to protect shop profitability against parts obsolescence and supply-chain gaps.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale automotive parts distribution", "Inventory management", "Business insight consulting", "Customized technician training", "Online parts catalog (MIC)", "Rapid Rewards loyalty program", "Shop management systems", "Marketing support", "Parts catalog management", "Consumer programs", "Safety data sheet provision"], "industries": ["Automotive repair and maintenance", "Professional automotive technicians", "Wholesale auto parts distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Local representative on-site, not offshore support", "Professional inventory management with obsolescence protection", "Bilingual English/Spanish service", "Value-added training, business tools, and marketing support", "Exclusive focus on professional technicians, not retail"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1963 -> db, / (homepage)", "Henderson, NV location at 1180 Center Point Drive -> / (homepage)", "Manager Scott Worrall -> / (homepage)", "Part of Grupo Gonher -> / (homepage footer)", "Distributes OE-sourced auto parts to professional technicians only -> / (homepage)", "Product lines: brakes, filters, batteries, belts, chemicals, hardware, motor oil, shop supplies, tire service, tools, wipers, PPE -> / (homepage)", "Services: inventory management, business insight, training, MIC catalog, Rapid Rewards, shop systems, marketing support -> / (homepage)", "Bilingual English/Spanish -> / (homepage)", "Corporate HQ Peachtree Corners, GA -> / (homepage footer)", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Mighty Auto Parts Nevada sources the highest quality auto parts from the world''s leading OE manufacturers, serving as the lynch-pin between manufacturers and only professional technicians from coast-to-coast.", "founded_year": "1963", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "Spanish"], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/mightyautoparts/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mighty-auto-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mike''s Metal Works operates from Bozeman, Montana, where founder Mike Winters established the shop in 1986 after years in roofing and sheet metal. The business draws on three generations of metalworking knowledge; a shop anvil passed down from Winters'' grandfather has been in the family for over a century.

The company produces custom architectural metalwork, specializing in copper, zinc, lead, and stainless steel roofing systems built with traditional techniques such as double-lock standing seam, flat seam, and soldered joints. A full-service fabrication shop houses shears, brakes, rolls, turners, punches, a forge, welders, plasma cutting, roll forming, and an English wheel, enabling production of cupolas, gutters, range hoods, and other custom pieces. Welding capabilities cover copper, steel, stainless steel, aluminum, and exotic alloys. The shop runs without computer-aided layout, relying on trammels, dividers, and rules, and employs only two or three workers to maintain personal oversight.

The firm''s work has been featured in Cowboys and Indians magazine.

Winters emphasizes a traditional, small-scale approach as the differentiator: time-tested hand tools, multi-generational expertise, and a lean crew ensure quality and responsive service on each project.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal fabrication", "Copper roofing (double-lock standing seam, flat seam, soldered)", "Zinc roofing", "Lead roofing", "Stainless steel roofing", "Custom architectural metalwork (cupolas, gutters, range hoods)", "Welding (copper, steel, stainless steel, aluminum, exotic alloys)", "Plasma cutting", "Roll forming", "English wheel forming", "Shearing", "Braking (press brake)", "Rolling", "Turning", "Punching", "Forging", "Hand layout (trammels, dividers, rules)", "Mobile positioning device fabrication/installation"], "industries": ["Architectural metalwork", "Roofing", "Custom metal fabrication"], "materials": ["Copper", "Zinc", "Lead", "Stainless steel", "Steel", "Aluminum", "Exotic alloys"], "equipment": ["Shears", "Brakes (press brakes)", "Rolls (slip rolls)", "Turners", "Punches", "Forge", "Welders", "Plasma cutting system", "Roll forming equipment", "English wheel", "Trammels", "Dividers", "Rules", "Anvil (family, over 100 years)", "Mobile positioning device (custom)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Traditional hand-craft methods using trammels, dividers, and rules with no computer layout", "Three generations of family metalworking knowledge and a century-old anvil", "Custom mobile positioning device for ergonomic roof installation", "Small crew of two to three workers for personal project oversight", "Full-service sheet metal shop with forge, English wheel, and plasma cutting"], "facts_used": ["Founded by Mike Winters in 1986 -> db, /, /about", "Location: Bozeman, Montana -> db, /, /about", "Specializes in copper, zinc, lead, stainless steel -> /, /about", "Three generations of knowledge, family anvil over a century -> /about", "Full service sheet metal shop equipment list -> /about", "Welding capabilities for copper, steel, stainless, aluminum, exotic metals -> /about", "Traditional techniques: double-lock standing seam, flat seam, solder -> /about", "Custom products: cupolas, gutters, range hoods -> /about", "No computer layout; uses trammels, dividers, rules -> /about", "Employs two or three select workers -> /about", "Testimonial from Robert Zahner, Zahner Company, Sun Valley Amphitheater project -> /about", "Mobile positioning device for ergonomic installation -> /about", "Published in Cowboys and Indians -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Mike''s Metal Works maintains a full service sheet metal shop with shears, brakes, rolls, turners, punches, forge, welders, plasma cutting, roll forming, and English Wheel.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "2-3", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mike-s-metal-works' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Mill End Store operates from two locations in the Portland metropolitan area: its original Milwaukie, Oregon site opened in 1918 and a Beaverton branch added in the 1980s. The business has remained family-owned throughout its history, beginning as one of the West Coast’s first worsted wool mills that supplied military uniforms during both world wars and provided yarn for early Jantzen knitted swimwear.

Today the company functions as a specialty fabric retailer with more than 50,000 square feet of combined retail space stocking designer runs, one-of-a-kind fabrics, trims, and notions. Inventory turns daily, and the store fulfills orders by phone and mail for customers worldwide, supplemented by a swatch service and special-order program.

The customer base spans professional costumers for film and television, nationally recognized fashion designers, interior designers, quilters, crafters, and novice sewists. Shoppers regularly travel from across the country to visit the physical stores, which are open Tuesday through Saturday.

