UPDATE companies SET description='Morton Solar, LLC was founded in 2006 by Brad Morton in Evansville, Indiana. After years as a controls engineer at Caterpillar''s mining truck plant in Decatur, Illinois, where he designed automated machinery for the CAT 797 mining truck, Morton established the company to advance solar energy adoption in the tri-state region.

The firm operates as a full-service solar and electrical contractor, delivering engineering, procurement, and construction (EPC) for residential, commercial, industrial, agricultural, and utility-scale photovoltaic systems. It also installs battery energy storage systems, including Tesla Powerwall and commercial BESS, EV charging infrastructure, and provides commercial and industrial electrical contracting through its parent company, Morton Electric, covering automation and controls, power distribution, panel building, and advanced manufacturing support. Notable installations include a 1.4 MW system for Vuteq in Princeton, a 2 MW array for AstraZeneca in Mount Vernon, and a 540 kW solar canopy for Orthopaedic Associates in Newburgh.

Morton Solar serves homeowners, businesses, farms, nonprofits, municipalities, schools, medical facilities, and industrial manufacturers across southern Indiana, western Kentucky, and southeastern Illinois. Its public-sector portfolio includes two of the nation''s first net-zero energy public buildings—Richardsville Elementary School and Chrisney Library—as well as projects for utilities and government agencies.

The company distinguishes itself through a values-driven model, holding B Corp certification and membership in the Amicus Solar Cooperative. Its team includes NABCEP-certified professionals and an in-house grant writer for USDA REAP grants, and it is an approved SREC vendor for the Illinois Shines program. Morton Solar has also advocated for policy changes that expanded net-metering and streamlined interconnection processes in Indiana.', certifications=ARRAY['B Corp Certification','NABCEP PV Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar EPC (Engineering, Procurement, Construction)", "Residential solar installation", "Commercial & industrial solar installation", "Utility-scale solar installation", "Battery energy storage systems (BESS) installation", "Tesla Powerwall installation", "EV charger installation", "Commercial & industrial electrical contracting", "Automation & controls", "Power distribution", "Panel building", "Advanced manufacturing support", "Solar repair, maintenance, & O&M", "Grant writing for USDA REAP Grant", "SREC vendor (Illinois Shines)"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Municipal", "Utility", "Government", "Nonprofit", "Medical", "Educational", "Manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified B Corporation", "Member of Amicus Solar Cooperative", "NABCEP PV Certified installation team", "Engineered two of the nation''s first net-zero public schools and libraries", "In-house grant writing for USDA REAP grants", "Illinois-approved SREC vendor"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2006 by Brad Morton -> db, /about-us", "Headquartered in Evansville, Indiana -> db", "Provides solar EPC, battery storage, electrical contracting -> /, /services", "Projects for Vuteq (1.4 MW), AstraZeneca (2 MW), Orthopaedic Associates (540 kW) -> /", "Certified B Corporation -> /", "NABCEP PV Certified -> /services", "Member of Amicus Solar Cooperati