UPDATE companies SET description='Mountain Meadow Wool Mill was founded in 2007 by Karen Hostetler in Buffalo, Wyoming. The mill emerged from a mission to preserve the ranching culture of the Great American West, where Basque sheepherders had established small ranches in the late 1800s. Declining wool prices over the preceding decades threatened those operations, prompting Hostetler and her partner to open a full-service mill that would offer fair prices to ranchers for their wool.

The mill handles the entire wool supply chain under one roof: it sources fleece directly from Wyoming ranches, then scours, cards, spins, and knits the fiber into finished goods. Operations include custom processing for outside growers, in-house spinning of yarn, and knitting of apparel, blankets, and home goods. The facility also runs an eco-friendly processing line and maintains a retail shop and wholesale program.

Primary customers are Wyoming sheep ranchers who sell their clip to the mill, as well as wholesale buyers and direct consumers seeking American-made wool yarn, knitting kits, baby blankets, beanies, and wearable art. The mill has supplied fiber for University of Wyoming branded products and collaborates with local artisans through its Legacy Yarn Guild.

Hostetler started the business to reverse the decline of the region’s wool economy and to keep processing jobs in Wyoming. The company emphasizes traceability from ranch to home, fair pricing for producers, and environmentally responsible methods that preserve wool’s natural softness and durability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wool processing", "Wool scouring and carding", "Wool spinning", "In-house knitting", "Wholesale wool yarn and products", "Retail sales of wool apparel and home goods", "Mill tours", "Fiber arts education (Legacy Yarn Guild)"], "industries": ["Agriculture (wool production)", "Textile manufacturing", "Apparel manufacturing", "Home furnishings manufacturing", "Craft and hobby supplies"], "materials": ["Wool", "Wyoming-grown wool", "Legacy Fleece"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Direct ranch-to-product oversight", "Fair pricing for rancher-supplied wool", "Eco-friendly processing methods", "In-house spinning and knitting", "Custom wool processing for outside growers"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2007 by Karen Hostetler -> db", "Headquarters in Buffalo, Wyoming -> db", "Mission to preserve ranching culture and offer fair prices to ranchers -> description", "Full-service mill with custom processing, spinning, and in-house knitting -> homepage", "Products include yarn, apparel, home goods, kits -> homepage", "Works with Wyoming ranchers (Legacy Fleece) -> homepage", "Eco-friendly processing -> homepage", "Offers mill tours and Legacy Yarn Guild -> homepage", "University of Wyoming branded products -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "full-service mill that offers fair prices to ranchers for their wool", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='mountain-meadow-wool-mill' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Murray Electronics Inc. was founded in 1996 in Murray, Kentucky. The company began as a provider of custom audio and video system design and installation for both commercial and residential clients.

The firm designs and installs a range of custom electronics including audio, video, automated systems, security, surveillance, controlled lighting, and communications. Its process moves from consultation and design through installation to ongoing service and support. The team comprises system designers, programmers, and installers who collaborate with builders, interior designers, and general contractors. Murray Electronics offers a wide range of equipment at various price points to meet specific design needs.

Murray Electronics serves commercial customers with surveillance, security, access control, audio/video, networking, and phone systems. On the residential side, it provides home theater, home automation, whole-home audio, security, central vacuum, and custom installation services. Clients include business owners, homeowners, and construction professionals.

