The shop specializes in steel fabrication, arc welding, and precision machining. Its team of fabricators and welders produces handcrafted components built to exact customer specifications, handling projects that range from structural steelwork to machined parts.

N.W. Metal Fabricators emphasizes its combined workforce experience of over 100 years in professional fabrication, positioning that depth of knowledge as a key differentiator. The company states that its products are handcrafted to meet exact specifications, reflecting a focus on precision and craftsmanship.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal fabrication", "Machining", "Welding", "Steel fabrication"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted products built to exact specifications", "Over 100 years of combined fabrication experience", "Steel fabrication and arc welding expertise"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986, headquarters Hermiston, Oregon -> db", "Services: metal fabrication, machining, welding -> db", "Handcrafted to exact specifications, over 100 years combined experience -> db", "Serves Hermiston, Umatilla County, Hinkle, Charleston -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our customers know they can count on our steel fabricators and arc welders to ensure products that are handcrafted to meet exact specifications.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='n-w-metal-fabricators-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='NU Packaging operates from Salt Lake City, Utah. The company was founded in 2001 by Jim, who had spent two decades in the packaging industry and wanted to bring a more creative, enjoyable approach to the business. It remains family-owned and operated. Jim passed away in June 2025, and the team continues to run the business according to his original vision.

NU Packaging functions as both a wholesale packaging distributor and a box manufacturer. Following the acquisition of a local box-making facility, the company produces custom-sized corrugated boxes on demand at its Salt Lake City plant. It also provides vendor-managed inventory (VMI) and stocking agreements backed by live inventory reporting updated every 12 hours. Delivery runs daily with next-day service to the Salt Lake and Utah Valleys, and twice weekly to Davis and Weber Counties with on-demand flexibility. The staff collectively holds over 120 years of packaging experience.

Its customer base includes technology firms in the Silicon Slopes corridor, manufacturers in Ogden and Davis County, and other organizations needing wholesale packaging supplies, custom corrugated designs, or automated packaging solutions.

Jim started the company to inject a sense of fun and creativity into packaging, emphasizing innovation, reliability, and a welcoming culture. NU Packaging differentiates itself through a local, human-staffed customer service team, on-demand manufacturing that cuts material waste and shipping costs, and a "Full Package" model that designs, manufactures, stocks, and delivers packaging under one roof.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale packaging distribution", "Custom corrugated box manufacturing", "Vendor managed inventory (VMI)", "Stocking agreements", "Live inventory reporting (12-hour updates)", "Next-day delivery (Salt Lake & Utah Valleys)", "Twice-weekly delivery (Davis & Weber Counties)", "Custom packaging design", "High-speed automation integration"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Next-day delivery for stocked items in Salt Lake & Utah Valleys; twice-weekly delivery to Davis & Weber Counties", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Next-day delivery to Salt Lake & Utah Valleys", "Twice-weekly delivery to Davis & Weber Counties with on-demand flexibility", "Vendor Managed Inventory (VMI) with live 12-hour inventory reporting", "Stocking Agreements reserving dedicated inventory in SLC warehouse", "Custom-sized box manufacturing on demand in Salt Lake City"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 by Jim -> /about", "Family-owned -> /about", "Headquarters Salt Lake City, Utah -> db", "Acquired local box manufacturing facility -> /", "Custom-sized box manufacturing on demand -> /", "VMI services and Stocking Agreements with live 12-hour reporting -> /", "Next-day delivery to Salt Lake & Utah Valleys -> /", "Twice-weekly delivery to Davis & Weber Counties -> /", "120 years collective packaging experience -> /", "Jim passed away June 2025 -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Northern Utah''s Premier Independent Packaging Distributor and Box Manufacturer", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nu-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='National Bushing & Parts Co. traces its roots to 1920 when Ray Riley and Aime Pouliot founded the company in Minneapolis, Minnesota. The pair began by manufacturing bronze bushings and distributing replacement parts for early automobiles such as Pierce Arrow, Packard, and Ford, as well as truck, bus, and tractor components.

Today the company operates as Automotive Parts Headquarters (APH), a wholesale distributor serving a network of more than 160 company stores and independent store customers across Minnesota, North Dakota, Wisconsin, and Michigan. A 160,000-square-foot distribution center in St. Cloud, opened in 2006, supports warehousing and logistics for the Auto Value brand. APH has been a member of the Aftermarket Auto Parts Alliance since 1986, leveraging the coalition’s purchasing power and branding.

The customer base includes professional installers and serious do-it-yourself buyers seeking automotive aftermarket parts, supplies, and service. Historically the catalog covered components for passenger cars, trucks, buses, and tractors; the current offering spans the full range of aftermarket repair parts sold through the Auto Value retail network.

