: [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='national-bushing-parts-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='National Content & Technology Cooperative (NCTC) is a not-for-profit cooperative headquartered in Overland Park, Kansas. Founded in 1984, the organization began with the goal of helping independent broadband and pay-TV providers become more competitive, smarter, and more efficient in building and maintaining coax and fiber networks. Its founding mission was to help members competitively acquire video programming and vital technologies needed to offer services that define their communities’ infrastructure.

The cooperative negotiates programming and streaming agreements with more than 200 TV networks on behalf of its 700-plus member companies, which collectively serve roughly one-third of all households and businesses in North America and U.S. territories. Its connectivity portfolio includes IP transit and transport, DDoS mitigation, analytics, SD-WAN, DNS, cloud, and CDN services. NCTC also offers video platform solutions and operates a group-purchasing marketplace that gives members a single point of contact for technology procurement, contract management, and supplier performance.

The cooperative’s members are independent communications service providers—broadband and pay-TV operators—ranging from small rural operators to larger regional players. Network providers and suppliers such as CommScope, eero, TiVo, Cogent Communications, Lumen, and Zayo Group work through NCTC as a gateway to reach this diverse member base. NCTC’s supplier directory lists dozens of approved and preferred partners across hardware, software, and professional services.

NCTC’s differentiating premise is that collective purchasing power enables members to secure deals they could not obtain individually. The cooperative emphasizes a streamlined, one-stop procurement process, defined service-level commitments, and ongoing technology innovation to help members remain profitable and sustainable in a rapidly changing industry.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Content programming negotiation", "Streaming service aggregation", "IP transit and transport", "DDoS mitigation", "Network analytics", "SD-WAN deployment", "DNS management", "Cloud services", "CDN services", "Video platform solutions", "Group purchasing and procurement", "Contract management", "Supplier performance management", "Partner relations and supplier directory", "Technology innovation consulting", "Marketplace operation"], "industries": ["Independent broadband service providers", "Pay-TV communications service providers", "Network infrastructure providers", "Telecommunications equipment suppliers", "Streaming content providers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Combined buying power across 700+ independent providers", "Single point of contact for technology procurement and contract management", "Not-for-profit cooperative structure focused on member profitability", "Access to 200+ programming networks and major streaming providers", "Connectivity suite including IP transit, DDoS mitigation, SD-WAN, and CDN"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1984 -> db", "Headquartered in Overland Park, Kansas -> db", "Not-for-profit cooperative -> /about", "700-plus member companies -> /about", "Members serve roughly one-third of households and businesses in North America and U.S. territories -> /about", "Negotiates with more than 200 TV networks and several streaming providers -> /", "Connectivity solutions include IP transit/transport, DDoS mitigation, analytics, SD-WAN, DNS, cloud and CDN services ->