UPDATE companies SET description='The company was founded in 2013 by Jason Fox, who initially launched the venture as an engineering and prototyping business. A lifelong interest in Japanese history and culture, combined with a background in machining and computer-aided design, eventually steered the firm toward the precise world of Japanese woodworking.

The studio specializes in traditional woodworking, furniture design, timber framing, and finish carpentry, producing items such as tokonoma alcoves, shoji doors, gates, and custom furniture pieces. Work is carried out using predominantly Japanese hand tools and techniques, and the shop also passes on those methods through woodworking classes and timber-frame workshops often led by guest masters. Project examples include a yellow cedar partition wall, a fir slab dining island, a walnut entry door, and a hexagonal hot tub.

Past projects range from a garden shed and a mountain home to a Kyoto-inspired tea room, a sushi counter, and a sauna, indicating a focus on high-quality, bespoke installations for both private and public environments.

Fox describes the company''s guiding principle as a covenant to "honor the tree," sourcing lumber directly when possible and favoring natural finishes. The design philosophy blends Japanese aesthetics with Shaker and Mid-Century Modern influences, aiming for what he calls "utilitarian elegance" — simple, clean forms that let the material speak for itself.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Traditional Woodworking", "Furniture Design", "Timber Framing", "Finish Carpentry", "Shoji Doors", "Tokonoma", "Woodworking Classes", "Timber Frame Workshops"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Yellow Cedar", "Fir", "Redwood", "American Hinoki", "Walnut", "Elm"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Utilizes predominantly Japanese hand tools and techniques", "Offers woodworking classes and timber-frame workshops taught by guest masters", "Sources lumber directly when possible and uses natural finishes", "Design philosophy of ''utilitarian elegance'' blending Japanese, Shaker, and Mid-Century Modern styles"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2013 by Jason Fox -> /about", "Located in Mercer, Maine -> /about", "Specializes in traditional woodworking, furniture design, timber framing, tokonoma, shoji doors, gates using Japanese tools -> /", "Offers woodworking classes and timber frame workshops -> /", "Design philosophy: honor the tree, utilitarian elegance -> /about", "Projects include yellow cedar partition walls, fir slab dining island, walnut entry door, hexagonal hot tub -> /", "Sources trees directly, uses natural finishes -> /about", "Founded as engineering and prototyping company -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Never Stop Building is a design-build studio located in central Maine. We specialize in traditional woodworking, furniture design, timber framing, tokonoma, shoji doors, and gates, utilizing predominantly Japanese tools and techniques.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='never-stop-building-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1988 in Randolph, Vermont, New England Precision Inc. operates an 80,000-square-foot manufacturing and tooling facility. The company began as a precision metal stamping specialist focused on brass and copper components.

Today the shop stamps a range of metals including brass, copper, aluminum, nickel, steel, and stainless steel. Its press line spans 18 to 280 tons with combined speed ranges, and the company maintains all tooling in-house to protect tool life and reduce costs. The facility houses both stamping and tool-and-die operations under one roof.

The company serves customers in building fire protection and hardware, automotive, aerospace, medical devices, and electrical sensors and controls. Its parts go into lock hardware, medical sensors, automotive controls, and aerospace components.

New England Precision emphasizes defect prevention and was an early adopter of ISO 9001 and the automotive IATF 16949 standard. Management describes its approach as versatility and flexibility, aiming to exceed expectations on every shipment while holding prices steady.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision metal stamping", "Brass stamping", "Copper stamping", "Aluminum stamping", "Nickel stamping", "Steel stamping", "Stainless steel stamping", "Tool and die making", "In-house tooling maintenance"], "industries": ["Building fire protection & hardware", "Automotive", "Aerospace", "Medical", "Electrical sensors and controls"], "materials": ["Copper", "Brass", "Aluminum", "Nickel", "Steel", "Stainless Steel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Press range from 18 to 280 tons", "In-house tooling maintenance and protection", "ISO 9001 and IATF 16949 certified", "Defect prevention focus", "Versatility and flexibility in production"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 -> db, /about", "Headquarters in Randolph, Vermont -> db, /", "80,000-square-foot manufacturing and tooling facility -> /, /about", "Specializes in precision metal stamping of brass and copper -> /, /about", "Also stamps aluminum, nickel, steel, stainless steel -> /", "Press range 18 to 280 tons -> /about", "In-house tooling maintenance -> /about", "Industries served: building fire protection & hardware, automotive, aerospace, medical, electrical sensors and controls -> /", "ISO 9001 certified -> /quality", "IATF 16949 certified -> /quality", "Focus on defect prevention -> /quality", "Materials: copper, brass, aluminum, nickel, steel, stainless steel -> /", "Company type: manufacturer -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "New England Precision, Inc. is a precision metal stamping company specializing in brass and copper metal stampings.", "founded_year": "1988", "emp