UPDATE companies SET description='New England Truck Design operates from Sterling, Massachusetts, where it was founded in 1977 by Kevin Lavin after his tenure at Wolf Coach building custom emergency vehicles.

The company designs and builds custom aluminum and stainless-steel truck bodies including dump, grain/chipper, flatbed, switch‑n‑go, fire apparatus, and specialty bodies for trucks ranging from pickups to 10‑wheelers. All fabrication is done in‑house: heavy‑walled perimeter angles, I‑beam cross members on 12‑inch centers, structural channel long sills, and plate floors up to 3/8‑inch thick. They also install BOSS snowplows, Rugby truck bodies, Torwel sanders, Protech toolboxes, fenders, lighting systems from Whelen, Federal Signal, and Trucklite, and hydraulic packages from Parker, Chelsea, and Permco.

Customers span municipal fleets (ambulances, fire trucks, brush trucks), construction and hauling contractors, military programs, and commercial operators needing grain or chipper bodies. The shop stocks emergency‑lighting components and provides full wiring and installation services for each build.

Lavin’s team emphasizes longevity over weight savings, using extruded structural sills instead of formed members and a proprietary linear cam latch that removes bell‑crank linkages, allowing higher toolbox mounting. In‑house electrical work and a policy of overbuilding for the work environment are cited as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom aluminum fabrication", "Custom stainless steel fabrication", "Truck body manufacturing (dump, grain/chipper, flatbed, switch-n-go, fire, specialty)", "Welding (heavy-walled perimeter angle, I-beam cross members, structural channel)", "CNC milling (board pockets)", "Hydraulic system installation and service", "Electrical wiring and installation", "Emergency lighting installation", "Snowplow installation", "Fender installation", "Toolbox and cab guard installation", "Custom switch panel fabrication", "Repair services"], "industries": ["Municipal/emergency vehicles", "Construction", "Hauling", "Military", "Commercial trucking", "Agriculture (grain/chipper)", "Landscaping (snowplows, sanders)"], "materials": ["Aluminum (5052)", "Aluminum sheet (.190)", "Aluminum plate (3/16, 1/4, 3/8)", "Stainless steel", "Structural steel channel", "Steel I-beams"], "equipment": ["BOSS snowplows", "Rugby truck bodies", "Torwel sanders", "Protech aluminum toolboxes", "Lifetime fenders", "WTI fenders", "Minimizer fenders", "Roadworks", "Double JJ Products", "Trucklite lighting", "Federal Signal lighting", "Whelen lighting", "Maxxima lighting", "PSE lighting", "Parker hydraulic components", "Commercial hydraulic components", "Chelsea hydraulic components", "Del hydraulic components", "Drum hydraulic components", "Permco hydraulic components", "LHA hydraulic components", "American Mobile Power hydraulic components"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Extruded structural sills instead of formed members for greater strength", "I-beam cross members on 12-inch centers with heavy-walled perimeter angle", "Proprietary linear cam latch for tailgates eliminating bell-crank linkages", "In-house wiring and installation of emergency lighting systems", "Overbuilt body construction prioritizing longevity over weight reduction"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1977 by Kevin Lavin -> db", "Headquarters Sterling, MA -> db", "Custom aluminum and stainless steel truck bodies -> /", "Dump, grain/chipper, flatbed, switch-n-go, fire, specialty bodies -> /", "Heavy-walled perimeter angle, I-beam cross members 12-inch centers -> /", "Linear cam latch for tailgates -> /", "In-house wiring and emergency lighting installation -> /", "BOSS snowplows, Rugby truck bodies, Torwel sanders, Protech toolboxes -> /", "Hydraulic systems from Parker, Chelsea, Permco, etc. -> /", "Materials: 5052 aluminum, .190 sheet, 3/16-3/8 plate, stainless steel -> /", "Industries: municipal, construction, military, commercial -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All of our bodies are constructed with a heavy walled perimeter angle. This allows deeper welding penetration for the cross members while still controlling distortion.", "founded_year": "1977", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-england-truck-design' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Farm Solar was founded in 2014 in Rogers, Arkansas, by Patrick Villines. A generational farm kid from Boxley Valley, Villines taught himself off-grid installation while homesteading in the early 2000s, then apprenticed with Rocky Grove Sun Company before earning his NABCEP certification and launching the locally owned business.

The company designs and installs custom solar energy systems for residential, commercial, and agricultural customers across Arkansas, Missouri, and Oklahoma. Its services span rooftop and ground-mount solar arrays, battery backup and off-grid power systems, commercial battery energy storage for peak shaving, EV charging infrastructure, generator installation, solar removal and reinstallation for reroofing projects, and panel cleaning. With a core team of six — including an operations manager, technical support specialist, project coordinator, and creative director — New Farm Solar has completed more than 500 installations since inception.

Customers range from homeowners seeking utility bill reduction to farms and businesses pursuing energy resilience and demand-charge savings. Recent projects include whole-home backup systems for rural properties, commercial peak-shaving installations that lower peak-demand charges, and EV charging deployments for both single-family homes and fleet operations. The firm also services existing arrays through its reroof and cleaning programs.

Villines started the company out of a passion for sustainability and a desire to provide honest, pressure-free guidance. New Farm Solar emphasizes tailored system design over one-size-fits-all packages, and it backs its work with long-term support and NABCEP-certified expertise.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar system design and installation", "Commercial solar system design and installation", "Battery backup system design and installation", "Off-grid power system design and installation", "Commercial battery energy storage (BESS) for peak shaving", "EV charging station installation", "Generator installation", "Solar removal and reinstallation (reroof services)", "Solar panel cleaning", "Energy consultation and system design"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural", "Energy storage", "Electric vehicle charging"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["NABCEP Certified installer", "500+ completed installations", "Locally owned with no high-pressure sales approach", "Custom system design tailored to each property", "Long-term support and service after installation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 -> db", "Headquarters Rogers, Arkansas -> db", "Founder Patrick Villines -> /about", "NABCEP Certified installer -> /", "500+ completed installations -> /", "Services: residential, commercial, battery backup, off-grid, generators, EV charging, commercial BESS, reroof, panel cleaning -> /, /services", "Team of six core members -> /about", "Serves Arkansas, Missouri, Oklahoma -> /", "Locally owned, no high-pressure sales -> /", "Custom system design and long-term support -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "As a NABCEP\u00ae Certified installer with 500+ completed installations, we specialize in residential and commercial solar, battery backup, off-grid systems, generators, EV charging, and commercial battery energy storage.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-farm-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Hampshire Accents Fine Crafts, LLC was founded in 1997 by Alfred Spitzer, Jr. in Manchester, New Hampshire. The shop began with the goal of providing true custom furniture and woodworking that could rival off-the-shelf offerings.

The company operates as a custom woodworking shop, building one-of-a-kind furniture and cabinetry piece by piece. Its process covers design, construction using hand-selected kiln-dried lumber, and finishing with a range of products including water- and oil-based stains, shellac, polyurethane, and lacquer. Projects span custom furniture, entertainment units, fireplace surrounds, wall units, built-ins, coffered ceilings, wainscoting, trim, crown moulding, and furniture refinishing and repair.

The shop serves residential clients, interior designers, and contractors. Interior designer Andrea Srinivas has collaborated on custom millwork including live-edge tables and cabinets, while homeowner George Samuels brought in a 30-year-old Spanish olive-wood table for hinge repair and refinishing. The company also works with contractors on built-ins and architectural details.

