ruction industry.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-hampshire-steel-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company traces its roots to the New Horizons Baking Company, which supplies large-scale baking solutions for a major quick-service restaurant brand, and the Genesis Baking Company, known for English muffins and soft rolls for iconic brands. While a founding year is not publicly disclosed, the organization has grown into a managed food solutions partner that integrates formulation, blending, packaging, and logistics under one roof.

NHFS provides contract food manufacturing and ingredient production, specializing in custom dry blends — such as seasoning systems, bakery blends, and multi-stage nutritional premixes — and ready-to-use liquid formulations including sauces, marinades, soups, dips, and concentrates. The facility operates at commercial scale with GFSI AA-graded, SQF-certified processes, supporting high-volume, long-running programs for foodservice, manufacturing, and retail channels. In-house capabilities span R&D and culinary development, specialty packaging tailored to throughput needs, and supply chain coordination backed by a dedicated transportation company, Metraco.

The company serves quick-service and fast-casual restaurant chains, food manufacturers and co-manufacturers, better-for-you and high-protein brands, nutrition and fortification producers, food aid and humanitarian organizations, and retail and ecommerce brands. Customers include a national baked goods partner, an iconic national QSR brand, and a global food aid organization, all of whom rely on NHFS for consistent flavor, reduced prep variability, and scalable production that protects proprietary formulas.

NHFS differentiates itself through a white-label model that safeguards customer intellectual property, an integrated team of food scientists and culinarians who collaborate from concept through commercialization, and an agile, responsive partnership structure that emphasizes direct communication and ownership of complex formulation challenges. The minority-owned, women-led leadership frames this approach as a continuation of a family legacy grounded in integrity and accountability.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF','GFSI AA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom dry blending", "Custom ready-to-use liquid blending", "R&D and product development", "Specialty packaging", "Supply chain optimization", "Custom vitamin and nutritional blending", "Contract food manufacturing", "Food ingredient manufacturing", "White label manufacturing", "Ingredient systems formulation", "Seasoning systems", "Nutritional premixes", "Functional ingredient formulations", "Packaging solutions", "Logistics and transportation (Metraco)"], "industries": ["QSR & Fast-Casual Brands", "Food Manufacturers & Co-Manufacturers", "Better-for-You & High-Protein Brands", "Nutrition & Fortification Producers", "Food Aid & Humanitarian Organizations", "Retail & Ecommerce Brands"], "materials": ["Food ingredients", "Seasonings", "Sauces", "Marinades", "Soups", "Dips", "Concentrates", "Vitamin premixes", "Protein systems", "Functional ingredients", "Nutritional blends"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["White-label manufacturing that protects customer formulas and IP", "GFSI AA-graded, SQF-certified facility", "Integrated R&D, culinary, quality, and operations teams", "In-house transportation and logistics via Metraco", "Minority-owned, women-led, family legacy"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Columbus, Ohio -> db", "Minority-owned, women-led, family legacy -> /", "Contract food manufacturing and food ingredient manufacturer -> /", "Custom dry blends, ready-to-use liquid blends, packaging, R&D, supply chain optimization, vitamin/nutritional blending -> /services", "Industries served: QSR & Fast-Casual Brands, Food Manufacturers & Co-Manufacturers, Better-for-You & High-Protein Brands, Nutrition & Fortification Producers, Food Aid & Humanitarian Organizations, Retail & Ecommerce Brands -> /", "GFSI AA-graded, SQF-certified facility -> /services", "In-house transportation company Metraco -> /", "White label food manufacturing partner protecting IP -> /services", "Family of brands: New Horizons Baking Company, Genesis Baking Company -> /", "Testimonials from national baked goods partner, iconic national QSR brand, global food aid organization -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "New Horizons Food Solutions (NHFS) is a contract food manufacturing and food ingredient manufacturer partner willing to lean in, adapt, and get it right.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Minority-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-horizons-food-solutions' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The New Mexico Independent Automobile Dealers Association (NMIADA) was established in Albuquerque, New Mexico, on August 21, 1962. Founded by a group of prominent independent dealers — Ross McCallister, Ralph Pool, Robert B. Gibson, Walter Gibson, and Sam Acquisto — the organization began as a 501(c)(6) professional association with the stated goal of advancing the interests of independent auto dealers while protecting the public through high business standards.

Today the association delivers a broad suite of services to its members, including dealer inspection and mobile VIN verification, bond and insurance programs, DOT compliance assistance, permitting and MVD title processing, marketing and branding consultation, consumer complaint resolution, and full back‑office management. It also conducts education and training programs, undertakes policy research, and maintains lobbying efforts at the local, state, and federal levels. The association invested in expanded facilities, technology, and staff following a 2017 strategic plan centered on serving, sharing, and supporting New Mexico’s independent dealers.

The primary constituency is New Mexico’s independent automobile dealers, though the association’s regulatory and consumer‑protection work also affects the broader automotive retail sector and the driving public. Its lobbying spans municipal, state, and national arenas, advocating for dealer‑friendly legislation and regulatory clarity.

The founders’ original mandate — to elevate dealer professionalism and safeguard consumers — remains the core differentiator. The 2017 strategic refresh reinforced a service‑first model that emphasizes hands‑off permitting, gold‑standard inspections, and a la carte support tailored to dealer operations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Dealer inspection services", "Bond and insurance services", "DOT compliance assistance", "Permitting services", "MVD title processing", "Mobile inspection and VIN verification", "Marketing, branding, and consultation services", "Consumer complaint resolution", "Full-service back-office management", "A la carte service options", "Lobbying at local, state, and federal levels", "Education and training programs for dealers", "Policy research and development"], "industries": ["Independent automobile dealers", "Automotive retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Gold Standard dealer inspection services", "Hands\u2011off, worry\u2011free permitting and MVD title processing", "Mobile inspection and VIN verification", "State and federal lobbying for independent dealers", "Full back\u2011office management and a la carte support"], "facts_used": ["Founded August 21, 1962 -> db", "Founders: Ross McCallister, Ralph Pool, Robert B. Gibson, Walter Gibson, Sam Acquisto -> page:/", "Headquarters: Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "501(c)(6) professional association -> page:/", "Services: dealer inspection, bond/insurance, DOT compliance, permitting, MVD title, mobile VIN, marketing consultation, consumer complaint resolution, back-office management -> page:/", "Lobbying at local, state, national levels -> page:/", "2017 strategic plan SERVE, SHARE & SUPPORT -> page:/", "Investments in facilities, technology, people -> page:/", "Website: http://www.nmiada.com/ -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "The New Mexico Independent