UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1996 in Bismarck, North Dakota, NewVision Security grew from a local security installer into a regional provider of integrated life-safety and security systems. The company is led by President and CEO Cameron Fleck, who began working in the industry as a teenager, and Chief Strategy Officer Chris Utter, a veteran of multiple security ventures.

NewVision designs, installs, services, and monitors security systems for commercial, residential, and institutional clients. Its core offerings include access control, video surveillance, intrusion detection, and fire alarm systems. The company maintains a local service department staffed by factory-certified technicians and operates a 24/7 monitoring center.

The client base spans small businesses, multi-site school districts, and private residences across the Dakotas and the broader Midwest. References include a multi-site school district installation and residential projects ranging from single-family homes to larger properties.

NewVision differentiates itself with a one-year warranty on parts and labor—double the industry’s typical 90-day coverage—and emphasizes direct, local support rather than distant corporate representatives. Membership in the Electronic Security Association and recognition on the 2026 SDM Top 100 list underscore its industry standing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Security system design", "Security system installation", "Security system support and maintenance", "24/7 alarm monitoring", "Access control systems", "Video surveillance / security cameras", "Intrusion / burglar alarm systems", "Fire alarm and fire protection systems"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Residential", "Education (K-12 school districts)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["1-year warranty on parts and labor (industry norm is 90 days)", "24/7 local monitoring center", "Factory-certified technicians for each installed system", "Member of the Electronic Security Association (ESA)", "Named to 2026 SDM Top 100 (out of 15,000+ companies)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 in Bismarck, ND -> db", "Headquarters Bismarck, ND -> db", "Services: design, installation, support, monitoring -> /services", "Core systems: access control, fire alarms, security cameras, interactive alarm systems -> /", "1-year warranty on parts and labor -> /", "24/7 monitoring -> /", "ESA member -> /", "SDM Top 100 2026 -> /", "Leadership: Cameron Fleck (President), Chris Utter (CSO), Gabe Goetz (Operations Manager), Jake Erickson (Director of Finance) -> /about", "Serves residential, commercial, school districts -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Security Systems are Our Full-Time Focus... We focus on access control, fire alarms, security cameras, and interactive alarm systems. Our comprehensive services range from initial consultation and installation to ongoing support and maintenance", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/newvision-security-nd/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='newvision-security' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Newfab Inc., headquartered in Auburn, Maine, traces its roots to 1955 when Northeast Welding and Fabrication was founded. The business started by producing wood stoves, concrete forms, railings, mounting brackets, and a variety of subcomponents for local customers.

Today the company operates as a full-service metal fabrication shop and contract manufacturer. Its capabilities span forming and welding, precision machining, painting and finishing, custom tooling and fixtures, product assemblies, turnkey equipment, and quality control and testing. Core product lines include high-temperature expansion joints and dampers, radio frequency transmission systems, machinery, and other custom metal assemblies, with engineering services supporting each project.

Newfab serves customers in energy, environmental, chemical, agricultural, alternative energy, military and defense, telecommunications, and industrial sectors. Its expansion joints and dampers are used in energy and environmental applications worldwide, while radio frequency transmission systems serve telecommunications clients, and custom machinery supports industrial and defense programs.

The company emphasizes proprietary manufacturing processes, specialized machinery, and dedicated tooling developed in-house to enable precise, efficient fabrication of complex components. It cites a commitment to quality, robustness, and on-time delivery, backed by decades of manufacturing heritage and a focus on rapid project turnaround.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract Manufacturing", "Forming & Welding", "Precision Machining", "Painting & Finishing", "Custom Tooling & Fixtures", "Product Assemblies", "Turnkey Equipment", "Quality Control & Testing", "Expansion Joints & Dampers", "Custom Sizing", "High Temperature Fabrication", "Heavy Duty Construction", "Engineering Services", "Process Development"], "industries": ["Alternative Energy", "Military & Defense", "Telecommunications", "Energy", "Environmental", "Chemical", "Agricultural", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary manufacturing processes and specialized machinery developed in-house", "Decades of manufacturing heritage since 1955", "Rapid project turnaround for custom engineered solutions", "Worldwide client reach across energy, defense, and industrial markets", "Commitment to quality, robustness, and on-time delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1955 -> /", "Headquarters in Auburn, Maine -> db", "Capabilities: Contract Manufacturing, Forming & Welding, Precision Machining, Painting & Finishing, Custom Tooling & Fixtures, Product Assemblies, Turnkey Equipment, Quality Control & Testing, Expansion Joints & Dampers, Engineering Services -> /", "Industries: Alternative Energy, Military & Defense, Telecommunications, Energy, Environmental, Chemical, Agricultural, Industrial -> db and /", "Acquisition of Design Fab in 2009 -> /", "Products: expansion joints, dampers, radio frequency transmission systems, machinery, custom assemblies -> /", "Proprietary manufacturing processes, specialized machinery, dedicated tooling -> /", "Commitment to quality, robustness, on-time delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "full-service metal fabrication shop and contract manufacturer", "founded_year": "1955", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='newfab-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Newport Sea Salt Co. operates from Newport, Rhode Island, where husband-and-wife team Matt and Tami Mullins founded the business after Matt’s 20-year career as a U.S. Naval Officer. The veteran-owned, woman-owned small business began with a desire to stay connected to the sea and to produce artisanal sea salt using traditional hand-harvesting methods.

The company hand-harvests seawater from Brenton Reef at high tide, filters it, and evaporates it in small batches to produce 100% natural flake sea salt with no additives. The product line includes plain flake salt and blended varieties such as Rosemary & Thyme, Butcher’s Blend, Bella Napoli, and Fire Salt. Production is small-scale, with the Mullins family and their sons Matthew and Connor comprising the crew.

Newport Sea Salt Co. sells directly to consumers at farmers markets and pop-up events across Rhode Island, and through retail partners including specialty food shops, cheese purveyors, and seafood markets in Rhode Island, New York, and California. The salt is also used by restaurant chefs and home cooks as a finishing salt.

The founders emphasize their unhurried, traditional process and the purity of their source water—an approved shellfish-growing area monitored by the Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management. They highlight that their salt retains trace minerals such as calcium, magnesium, and potassium, and contains no anti-caking agents, bleach, or iodine.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand harvesting of seawater", "Small-batch sea salt production", "Filtration", "Blending of flavored sea salts"], "industries": ["Food service", "Retail", "Specialty food"], "materials": ["Seawater", "Sea salt", "Herbs and spices"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-harvested from Brenton Reef at high tide only", "No anti-caking agents, bleach, or iodine added", "Retains trace minerals (calcium, magnesium, potassium)", "Small-batch, unhurried traditional process", "Veteran-owned and woman-owned family business"], "facts_used": ["Location: Newport, Rhode Island -> db", "Founders: Matt and Tami Mullins -> /about-us", "Ownership: veteran-owned, woman-owned, small business -> / (home page)", "Process: hand-harvesting seawater from Brenton Reef at high tide, filtration, small-batch evaporation -> / (home page) and /about-us", "Products: plain flake salt and blended varieties (Rosemary & Thyme, Butcher\u2019s Blend, Bella Napoli, Fire Salt) -> / (home page)", "Crew includes sons Matthew and Connor -> /about-us", "Sales channels: farmers markets, pop-up events, retail partners in RI, NY, CA -> / (home page)", "Source water: approved shellfish-growing area monitored by RI Dept. of Environmental Management -> /about-us", "No anti-caking agents, bleach, or iodine; retains trace minerals -> / (home page) and /about-us", "Certification: VETERAN OWNED -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our small veteran owned artisanal sea salt company follows the traditional and unhurried process of crafting small batches of 100% pure and natural sea salt.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Woman-owned", "Small business", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='newport-sea-salt-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Nextern is headquartered in Maple Grove, Minnesota. Founded in the early 2000s as an engineering and manufacturing partner for industrial components, the company shifted its focus to medical device electromechanical systems in 2016. In 2022, it acquired NPX Precision Technologies, adding nitinol and specialty alloy expertise, and consolidated product development into its new Maple Grove headquarters in 2024.

The company provides vertically integrated medical device development and manufacturing across four pillars: product development, manufacturing, precision technologies (NPX), and consulting services. Its capabilities span design-for-manufacturability, phase-gate development, agile sprints, nitinol shape-setting, laser cutting and welding (±0.0005″ tolerance), catheter shaft assembly, braiding, coiling, tip forming, and regulatory, clinical, and quality consulting. Operations run across five global sites: Maple Grove (HQ, development, manufacturing), Cartago, Costa Rica (manufacturing), Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam (manufacturing), Kenosha, Wisconsin (precision components), and Shenzhen, China (strategic sourcing).

Nextern serves OEMs, clinicians, and innovators in the medical device sector, with deep clinical market expertise in peripheral vascular (specialty wires, thrombectomy systems, renal denervation), interventional cardiology (delivery catheters, IVL catheters, balloon catheters), neuromodulation (pulse generators, implantable leads, wearable neurostim), electrophysiology (PFA generators, RF generators, ablation catheters), and structural heart (transcatheter delivery, implant frames, occlusion devices).

The company’s stated mission is to partner across the entire product lifecycle to solve patient needs and improve lives. Its differentiation rests on a vertically integrated model that embeds manufacturability from day one, a BioSimulation Lab for realistic device testing, and a phase-gate process designed to eliminate uncertainty early. The 2026 launch of consulting services extends its reach into regulatory strategy, clinical evidence, quality systems, and lifecycle management.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','21 CFR Part 820','ISO 14971:2019']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical device product development", "Medical device manufacturing", "Design-for-manufacturability (DFM)", "Phase-gate development process", "Agile sprints", "Nitinol shape-setting and heat treatment", "Laser cutting (wet/dry tube, flat sheet)", "Precision welding", "Electropolishing", "Catheter shaft assembly", "Braiding and coiling", "Complex tip forming", "Integrated sub-assembly", "Rapid R&D prototyping", "Concept validation", "Finished device assembly", "Line transfers", "Supply chain management", "Sterilization", "Warehousing", "Regulatory pathway planning", "FDA submissions (510(k), etc.)", "EU MDR technical documentation", "Clinical evaluation plans and reports"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Peripheral vascular", "Interventional cardiology", "Neuromodulation", "Electrophysiology", "Structural heart"], "materials": ["Nitinol", "Specialty alloys", "Metals (for medical devices)"], "equipment": ["Rofin StarCut laser system", "Femto laser system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.0005 in", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated product development and manufacturing under one roof", "Phase-gate development process with agile sprints", "BioSimulation Lab for realistic hydrodynamic device testing", "Design-for-manufacturability embedded from day one", "Global ISO 13485:2016 certified manufacturing footprint"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Maple Grove, Minnesota -> /", "Founded in early 2000s as industrial components partner -> /about", "Shift to medical device electromechanical systems in 2016 -> /about", "Acquisition of NPX Precision Technologies in 2022 -> /about", "Consolidation of product development into Maple Grove HQ in 2024 -> /about", "Launch of Consulting Services in 2026 -> /about", "Four service pillars: product development, manufacturing, precision technologies, consulting -> /capabilities", "Global sites: Maple Grove, Cartago, Ho Chi Minh City, Kenosha, Shenzhen -> /", "Clinical markets: peripheral vascular, interventional cardiology, neuromodulation, electrophysiology, structural heart -> /", "ISO 13485:2016 certification across sites -> /quality", "21 CFR Part 820 and ISO 14971:2019 standards -> /quality", "Nitinol shape-setting, laser cutting, welding, catheter assembly capabilities -> /capabilities", "\u00b10.0005\u2033 tolerance on Rofin StarCut and Femto systems -> /capabilities", "BioSimulation Lab for realistic device testing -> /capabilities", "Design-for-manufacturability from day one -> /capabilities", "Phase-gate process with agile sprints -> /capabilities", "Mission: partner to solve patient needs and improve lives -> /about", "Vision: benchmark for excellence and innovation in medical device partnership -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Nextern partners with OEMs, clinicians, and innovators to design, develop, and manufacture world-class medical devices across the full product lifecycle.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nextern' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The business remains family-owned, now led by the fourth generation of the Mouskondis family, and conducts its operations according to the Greek principle of philotimo — a commitment to honorable service to customers, employees, and the community.

The company functions as a broadline foodservice distributor across six territories in the Intermountain West. It maintains 16.7 million square feet of temperature-controlled warehouse space and stocks more than 14,000 unique products, ranging from fresh produce and center-of-plate proteins to canned goods, beverages, non-food supplies, and flowers. A fleet of over 100 climate-controlled tractors and trailers, equipped with scan-based picking and delivery tracking, supports daily distribution to customer sites.

Customers include independently owned restaurants, regional and national chains, healthcare facilities, government agencies, and educational institutions. The company fields dedicated teams for healthcare nutrition compliance, government and education procurement regulations, and chain-restaurant consistency programs. It also provides access to 1,800-plus Markon produce items, next-day specialty meat and fish kits, and more than 20 exclusive private-label brands.

Leadership emphasizes that family ownership enables agility and long-term stability compared with larger corporate distributors. The firm reinvests in community food donations, recycling initiatives, and local events, framing its scale and service breadth as tools to sustain the regional food ecosystem rather than merely to expand market share.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Broadline foodservice distribution", "Temperature-controlled warehousing", "Refrigerated and climate-controlled fleet delivery", "Scan-based order picking and delivery confirmation", "Real-time shipment tracking (Where''s My Truck)", "Custom foodservice program development", "Exclusive brand and private-label procurement", "Markon produce program (1,800+ items)", "Next-day specialty meat and fish kits", "Healthcare nutrition and regulatory compliance support", "Government and education procurement solutions", "Industry data and market insights", "Customer account management and on-site consultation"], "industries": ["Restaurant foodservice (independent and chain)", "Healthcare foodservice", "Government foodservice", "Education foodservice", "Institutional foodservice"], "materials": ["Fresh produce", "Center-of-plate proteins (meat, poultry, seafood)", "Canned and dry goods", "Beverages", "Non-food supplies", "Frozen foods", "Flowers"], "equipment": ["Climate-controlled tractor trailers (100+ fleet)", "Refrigerated loading docks", "Warehouse temperature control zones", "Scan pick and scan delivery systems", "Where''s My Truck tracking technology"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned independence allows faster adaptation than corporate giants", "16.7 million sq ft of temperature-controlled warehouse space across 6 territories", "Fleet of 100+ climate-controlled trucks with real-time tracking", "Exclusive access to 1,800+ Markon produce items and 20+ private-label brands", "Dedicated teams for healthcare, government, and education compliance"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1939 by Nicholas Mouskondis -> /about-us", "Family-owned, fourth generation involvement -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Salt Lake City, Utah -> db", "6 statewide territories -> /", "16.7 million sq ft warehouse space -> /", "14,000+ unique products stocked -> /", "Fleet of over 100 trucks and trailers -> /services", "Temperature-controlled warehouses, refrigerated loading docks, climate-controlled trailers -> /services", "Scan pick and scan delivery, Where''s My Truck technology -> /services", "Serves independent restaurants, national chains, institutions -> /", "Dedicated healthcare, government, education teams -> /services", "Markon produce program (1,800+ items) -> /services", "Next-day meat and fish kits -> /services", "20+ exclusive brands -> /services", "National partnerships with Dining Alliance and DMA -> /services", "Philotimo philosophy -> /about-us", "CEO Nicole Mouskondis -> /about-us", "Instagram @nicholasandco -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "As one of the only independently-owned broadline foodservice providers in the Mountain West", "founded_year": "1939", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://instagram.com/nicholasandco"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nicholas-and-company-salt-lake-city' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Nihm Electronic Solutions was founded in 2010 by James Bench in Las Vegas, Nevada. The company began as a contract manufacturer focused on custom wire harnesses and electronic circuit board assemblies, aiming to support the quick-turn, mixed-volume needs of OEMs and other contract manufacturers.

Today, Nihm produces wire harnesses, cable assemblies, printed circuit board assemblies (PCBA) using surface-mount technology, and 3D-printed prototypes via FDM and stereolithography. The shop also offers material engraving on metal, glass, wood, plastic, and 3D-printed parts through a partnership with Benchmarx Engraving. Operations run with no minimum or maximum order quantities, accommodating small runs and prototype quantities alike.

The company serves the transportation, medical, robotics, gaming, and communications industries. Its customer base includes original equipment manufacturers and fellow contract manufacturers seeking design-build services, reverse engineering, and first-article inspection.

Nihm differentiates itself with 100% testing on every unit, IPC 610/620-certified assemblers, a Komax Alpha 530 automated wire processor with crimp-force monitoring, and a DI water polishing system for fiber-optic cables. The quality program includes cross-section analysis, CPK process-capability tracking, and CAMI Research computer-guided testers that record pass/fail data for each harness.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS Directive 2002/95/EC','IPC 610','IPC 620','IPC 160']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire harness / cable assembly", "PCBA / SMT (surface-mount technology)", "3D modeling (FDM and SLA)", "Material engraving (metal, glass, wood, plastic, 3D prints)", "Reverse & concurrent engineering", "Custom wire, harness, and circuit board fabrication", "Prototyping", "First article inspection", "Troubleshooting & problem solving", "Fiber optic assembly (DI water polishing)", "Cross-section analysis", "CPK process capability analysis", "CAMI Research computer-guided cable testing", "RoHS compliance", "IPC 610/620 standards compliance"], "industries": ["Transportation", "Medical", "Robotics", "Gaming", "Communications"], "materials": ["Metal", "Glass", "Wood", "Plastic", "3D prints"], "equipment": ["Komax Alpha 530", "DI Water Polishing System", "FDM 3D printers", "SLA 3D printers", "CAMI Research cable testers", "Microscope inspection equipment"], "volume": "No minimum or maximum orders; small runs supported", "lead_time": "Quick turnarounds; lightning-quick deliveries", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum or maximum order quantities", "100% testing on every product", "Komax Alpha 530 automated wire processing with crimp-force monitoring", "DI water polishing system for fiber-optic cables", "Design-build services including diagramming and specifications preparation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2010 by James Bench in Las Vegas, Nevada -> db, /", "Contract manufacturer of custom wire harnesses and electronic circuit board assemblies -> /", "Services: wire h