UPDATE companies SET description='The New Jersey Cable and Internet Association (NJCIA) is headquartered in Trenton, New Jersey. Founded in 1965 as a voluntary trade organization, it serves as the collective voice for the state''s major cable telecommunications providers. The association operates under a board of directors drawn from its member companies.

NJCIA does not manufacture products; rather, it provides industry representation, government affairs advocacy, and economic research on behalf of its members—Comcast Cable Communications, Altice USA (operator of the Optimum brand), and Charter Communications (operator of the Spectrum brand). The association reports that its members collectively contribute $12.6 billion in economic impact to New Jersey and sustain approximately 75,975 direct and indirect jobs across all 12 congressional districts. Activities include advocating for broadband infrastructure investment, supporting federal programs such as the Affordable Connectivity Program, and publishing industry data.

The association serves the cable telecommunications, broadband internet, video services, and mobile communications industries in New Jersey. Its work benefits residents and businesses statewide by promoting network expansion and connectivity. As a state chapter affiliated with the National Cable & Telecommunications Association (NCTA), NJCIA coordinates with national policy efforts.

The organization was established to unify the cable industry''s voice in Trenton and to demonstrate the sector''s economic value to policymakers and the public. Member companies state that continued infrastructure investment is essential to meeting growing demand for high-quality broadband, video, and mobile services.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industry representation and advocacy", "Government affairs and regulatory engagement", "Economic impact research and reporting", "Member services and board governance", "Public policy coordination with NCTA", "Broadband infrastructure investment advocacy", "Affordable Connectivity Program support"], "industries": ["Cable telecommunications", "Broadband internet services", "Video programming distribution", "Mobile communications", "Trade associations"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Represents three major cable providers: Comcast, Altice USA, Charter Communications", "Documents $12.6 billion annual economic impact and 75,975 jobs in New Jersey", "Board governed by senior government affairs executives from each member company", "Advocates for broadband infrastructure investment and federal affordability programs", "Affiliated with the National Cable & Telecommunications Association (NCTA)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 as voluntary trade organization -> db, /, /about-us", "Headquarters Trenton, New Jersey -> db", "Name: New Jersey Cable and Internet Association (NJCIA) -> /, /about-us", "Represents Comcast, Altice USA, Charter Communications -> /, /about-us", "Economic impact $12.6 billion, 75,975 jobs -> /", "Board members: Tony Bawidamann (Comcast), Brian Quinn (Altice USA), Rodney S. Capel (Charter), Elizabeth Murray (Comcast), Stephanie Kosta (Comcast) -> /, /about-us", "Affiliated with National Cable & Telecommunications Association (NCTA) -> /", "Supports Affordable Connectivity Program -> /", "Services: broadband, video, mobile connectivity -> /, /about-us", "Website cablenj.org -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Founded in 1965 as a voluntary trade organization, NJCIA companies are key drivers of economic growth, innovation, and technological advancement.", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nj-cable-telecommunications' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Norco Precision, a sheet metal fabricator based in Minneapolis, Minnesota, traces its roots to 1976. The current iteration was launched in 2003 by Phil Nori, a metal fabrication veteran, with a mission to provide fabrication solutions and customer service. In 2023, ownership expanded to include Brandon Vannelli as president and Matt Hansen as co-owner, growing the team from its original two people to seven.

The company operates as a full-service sheet metal fabricator with in-house capabilities including laser cutting (Mitsubishi 8kW fiber laser), shearing (10'' x 1/4" hydraulic shear), forming (up to 12 feet, 170 tons), welding (TIG, MIG, spot, stud), punching, deburring, hardware insertion, and assembly. It also coordinates with local partners for machining, painting, plating, grinding, and additional punching. The shop handles steel, aluminum, and stainless steel up to 1/4-inch thick.

