UPDATE companies SET description='North Alabama Fabricating Company (NAFCO) is a structural steel fabricator headquartered in Birmingham, Alabama. Founded in 1954 by World War II veteran John Parrish, the business began as a structural detailing specialist and expanded into engineering, fabrication, and erection of complex steel projects. It remains a third-generation, family-owned operation under the Parrish family.

The company provides a full range of steel services — structural and industrial fabrication, erection, OEM subassemblies, in-house detailing (using Tekla and SDS/2), engineering, preconstruction design-assist, turnkey EPC for bulk material handling, sophisticated shop-applied coatings, and shop-applied fireproofing. NAFCO operates three fabrication sites in Alabama and a Chicago-based engineering division, Wolf Point Engineers & Contractors.

NAFCO serves power generation, commercial construction, aviation, material handling, warehousing, industrial plants, waste recycling, forestry, construction equipment, pulp and paper, aggregate mining, and heavy minerals. Concrete project examples include Schenck Silos, Naheola Biomass Ductwork, Second Line Stages Expansion, CPS Energy, Cliff’s Oak Grove, Cliff’s Bloom Lake, Bryant Denny Stadium renovations, and the Birmingham News Building.

