UPDATE companies SET description='Norwood Medical operates from a 700,000-square-foot manufacturing campus in Dayton, Ohio. The company traces its roots to 1926 when it began as a tool and die shop. A local businessman who had worked at the firm since 1950 purchased the business with a partner in 1981, and by the 1990s the operation had evolved into component manufacturing. Medical component manufacturing and assembly became its sole focus in the early 2000s. In 2021, Norwood was acquired by the Heraeus Group, a family-owned German technology group, preserving its family-oriented culture.

The company provides end-to-end contract manufacturing for medical devices, offering more than 30 in-house engineering and production capabilities. Core processes include CNC milling and turning (horizontal, vertical, and 5-axis), CNC Swiss machining, metal injection molding (MIM) with in-house feedstock formulation, insert injection molding, electrical discharge machining (wire and RAM), electrochemical machining (ECM), precision metal stamping, and water-jet cutting. Value-added post-processing covers laser marking and welding, polishing, electropolishing, heat treating, coating (PTFE dry film, sodium stearate, siliconization), ultrasonic cleaning, overmolding, and passivation. Testing, assembly, and packaging are performed in controlled environments supported by nine on-site quality labs. The campus houses over 800 CNC machines and supports production volumes from prototype to full-scale runs, with products used in more than 13 million surgeries annually.

Norwood serves the medical device industry, focusing on cardiovascular, minimally invasive surgery (MIS), orthopedics, robotic-assisted surgery (RAS), and surgical technologies. Its customers include well-known medical device OEMs that rely on the company for complex robotic instruments, energy-sealing devices, and other critical components.

The company emphasizes its vertically integrated model, long-term ownership perspective, and quality mindset as differentiators. It reinvests 3% of revenue annually in automation, maintains a 95% customer retention rate, and operates nine in-house metrology labs equipped with CMM, CT scanning, optical inspection, and laser scanning systems. A dedicated regulatory and compliance department ensures adherence to ISO 13485:2016, FDA 21 CFR 820, and ISO 14971:2019 standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','FDA 21 CFR 820','FDA registered','ISO 14971:2019']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Program management", "Rapid prototyping", "In-house tool shop", "Tooling & machining fixturing", "Die manufacturing", "Mold making", "Custom machine design, manufacturing & programming", "CNC milling & turning (horizontal, vertical, 5-axis)", "CNC Swiss machining", "Metal Injection Molding (MIM)", "Insert injection molding", "In-house feedstock formulation", "High-capacity pusher furnaces", "Electrical discharge machining (EDM) - wire and RAM", "Precision metal stamping (coining & forming)", "Electrochemical machining (ECM)", "Water-jet cutting", "Laser marking & welding", "Polishing & blasting (bead blast, belt & hard polishing)", "Electropolishing", "Heat treating", "Coating (PTFE dry film, sodium stearate, siliconization)", "Ultrasonic cleaning", "Overmolding", "Passivation", "Material testing", "Device testing", "Material analysis", "Metallurgical analysis", "Quality control/quality labs", "Fully automated inspection", "Assembly & packaging (manual & mechanical)", "Controlled environments for assembly"], "industries": ["Cardiovascular", "Minimally invasive surgery (MIS)", "Orthopedics", "Robotic-assisted surgery (RAS)", "Surgical technologies", "Medical device"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["800+ CNC machines", "State-of-the-art CNC mills", "Multi-axis lathes", "Advanced Swiss machines", "MIM molding machines", "High-capacity pusher furnaces", "Wire and RAM EDM machines", "State-of-the-art ECM machines", "Water-jet cutting machines", "Coordinate measuring machines (CMM)", "CT scanning", "Optical inspection systems", "Laser scanning", "Robotics, vision systems, laser marking, cutting, and welding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated campus with >30 in-house capabilities", "3% of revenue reinvested in automation each year", "95% customer retention rate", "13 million surgeries supported annually", "9 in-house quality labs with advanced metrology"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1926 as tool and die shop -> /about-us", "Purchased in 1981 by local businessman who worked there since 1950 -> /about-us", "Medical focus early 2000s -> /about-us", "Acquired by Heraeus Group in 2021 -> /about-us", "700,000 sq ft campus in Dayton, Ohio -> /", "800+ CNC machines -> /", "13M surgeries supported annually -> /about-us", "95% customer retention -> /about-us", ">30 in-house capabilities -> /", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> /quality", "FDA 21 CFR 820 compliant -> /quality", "ISO 14971:2019 compliant -> /quality", "Industries: Cardiovascular, MIS, Orthopedics, RAS, Surgical technologies -> /", "Capabilities: CNC milling, Swiss, MIM, EDM, ECM, stamping, water-jet, laser, polishing, electropolishing, heat treating, coating, passivation, assembly, testing -> /capabilities", "Automation investment 3% of revenue -> /capabilities", "Family-owned culture -> /about-us", "9 in-house quality labs with CMM, CT scanning, optical inspection, laser scanning -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Medical component manufacturing and assembly became Norwood''s sole focus in the early 2000s.", "founded_year": "1926", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug=